WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.400
Speaker 1: Well, we suspected it might happen&nbsp;
because of the increasingly uncontrolled spread of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.400 --> 00:00:10.480
the Delta variant and the resurgence in covid-19&nbsp;
cases, and it is happening, the CDC coming out&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:10.480 --> 00:00:16.800
with new mass guidelines yesterday. We are going&nbsp;
backwards. The masks are going back on in many,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:16.800 --> 00:00:23.360
many places and seemingly overnight. I'm already&nbsp;
seeing more masks just walking around. And yes,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:23.360 --> 00:00:31.520
this is even for vaccinated people. We're going to&nbsp;
look at the new guidelines and I am going to sort&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:31.520 --> 00:00:39.760
of couch it all in saying the situation has not&nbsp;
really changed that dramatically for vaccinated&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:39.760 --> 00:00:43.840
people, although it has changed and it's&nbsp;
important to understand the ways in which it has.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.640 --> 00:00:52.240
But this is continuing to increasingly be a virus&nbsp;
that is being spread by unvaccinated people,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:52.240 --> 00:00:59.440
which is disproportionately seriously affecting&nbsp;
unvaccinated people. And that, for now,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:59.440 --> 00:01:03.520
appears to be the way it is going to continue.&nbsp;
But that doesn't mean, given what's going on,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:04.320 --> 00:01:09.840
that vaccinated people shouldn't take precautions&nbsp;
in certain places. So let's look at the new CDC&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:09.840 --> 00:01:16.560
guidelines updated yesterday when you've&nbsp;
been fully vaccinated. OK, if you are fully&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:16.560 --> 00:01:21.120
vaccinated, you can participate in many of the&nbsp;
activities that you did before the pandemic&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:21.680 --> 00:01:27.280
to maximize protection from the Delta variant&nbsp;
and prevent possibly spreading it to others.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:27.920 --> 00:01:34.720
Wear a mask indoors in public. If you are in an&nbsp;
area of substantial or high transmission, that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:34.720 --> 00:01:40.640
is a major change. Whereas before the position&nbsp;
was if you're vaccinated, you don't really need&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:40.640 --> 00:01:46.720
to wear a mask anywhere. The new guidelines&nbsp;
are if you're vaccinated, but you're indoors&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:47.360 --> 00:01:51.840
in public, meaning not with five other people&nbsp;
whose vaccination status, you know, but if&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:51.840 --> 00:01:58.800
you're in public, indoors and in an area of high&nbsp;
transmission, which you can look at, at a county&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:58.800 --> 00:02:04.960
by county level, substantial or high transmission,&nbsp;
the new recommendation is to wear a mask for me.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:04.960 --> 00:02:10.800
What does that mean? Well, that means when I go to&nbsp;
the grocery store, the mask is going back on. It&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:10.800 --> 00:02:15.200
goes on to say the new guidelines wearing a mask&nbsp;
is most important if you have a weakened immune&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:15.200 --> 00:02:20.720
system or if because of your age or an underlying&nbsp;
medical condition, you are at increased risk for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:20.720 --> 00:02:26.240
severe disease, or if someone in your household&nbsp;
has a weakened immune system, is at increased&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:26.240 --> 00:02:31.520
risk for severe disease or is unvaccinated,&nbsp;
if this applies to you or your household,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:31.520 --> 00:02:35.840
you might choose to wear a mask regardless&nbsp;
of the level of transmission in your area.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:36.640 --> 00:02:43.440
You should continue to wear a mask where required&nbsp;
by laws, rules, regulations or local guidance.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:44.000 --> 00:02:51.120
So this is a significant change and we are seeing&nbsp;
the spike. I mean, if you look at the US case&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:51.120 --> 00:02:56.960
numbers, you will see that starting, oh, I don't&nbsp;
know, right around June 22nd about them. About&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:56.960 --> 00:03:03.040
a month ago, after getting down below 10000 cases&nbsp;
per day, cases started to go up, up, up, including&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:03.040 --> 00:03:11.280
even some sixty five thousand case days now up&nbsp;
to an average of about 57000 cases per day. Now,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:11.280 --> 00:03:18.080
what's the hope here? The hope is that much like&nbsp;
we are starting to see in some other countries,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:18.080 --> 00:03:24.000
for example, if you look at the U.K., which was&nbsp;
essentially one of the hubs of the Delta variant,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:24.640 --> 00:03:32.320
we have already apparently hit the peak of cases&nbsp;
in the U.K. that the peak in the U.K. of Delta&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:32.320 --> 00:03:38.480
seems to have happened around July 22nd and&nbsp;
they are now down from about 46000 cases a day&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:38.480 --> 00:03:44.560
to about thirty two thousand. That's a significant&nbsp;
reduction. The hope is that what is now a sort of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:44.560 --> 00:03:49.920
leveling out, as you can see over the last&nbsp;
few days, the cases aren't continuing to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:49.920 --> 00:03:54.800
increase in the U.S. They're sort of flattening&nbsp;
out. The hope would be we are now going to be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:55.600 --> 00:03:59.840
on the decline, but we don't know if we&nbsp;
are. And part of that depends, of course,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:00.480 --> 00:04:06.480
on taking precautions. So let's not go crazy&nbsp;
one way or the other. I think there's a lot of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:06.480 --> 00:04:12.960
hyperbole on both sides here. And I'm not playing&nbsp;
a both sides game. The people responsible for this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:12.960 --> 00:04:16.880
are overwhelmingly the unvaccinated people&nbsp;
and the people taking no precautions.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:16.880 --> 00:04:21.440
But the reactions have been sort of extreme on&nbsp;
both sides. There's one side that two months ago&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:21.440 --> 00:04:25.600
said the pandemic is over. Many of these people&nbsp;
were never wearing masks. Many of these people are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:25.600 --> 00:04:30.640
still not vaccinated. And they're going back. And&nbsp;
and to quote Dr. Anthony Fauci, letting it rip,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:30.640 --> 00:04:35.280
that's an extreme reaction on one side because&nbsp;
it's clearly not over. On the other side are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:35.280 --> 00:04:41.120
the people who are seeing this and now saying we&nbsp;
are back to the pre vaccine, uncontrolled spread&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:41.120 --> 00:04:47.760
era. The truth is that for the Delta variant, if&nbsp;
you're vaccinated, you're very well protected.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:48.640 --> 00:04:52.240
And that protection is bolstered by&nbsp;
people around you being vaccinated now,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:52.800 --> 00:05:01.120
just like with the flu, there are people who&nbsp;
are vaccinated who will who are otherwise&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:01.120 --> 00:05:06.960
mostly healthy, who will get what's called a break&nbsp;
through case, and they will end up hospitalized&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:06.960 --> 00:05:11.520
and a few of them are going to die. And that's a&nbsp;
terrible and tragic thing. But it's important to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:11.520 --> 00:05:18.240
remember that that also happens with the flu.&nbsp;
And we that doesn't mean we ignore this fact,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:18.240 --> 00:05:22.320
but it also doesn't mean that we all of a&nbsp;
sudden believe there's no protection. And&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:22.320 --> 00:05:29.680
we're going back to the pre vaccine covid era.&nbsp;
The truth is that for the most part, you are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:29.680 --> 00:05:33.520
quite well protected. If you were vaccinated,&nbsp;
you are really unlikely to get very sick.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:34.160 --> 00:05:38.960
You are really unlikely to die. However, you could&nbsp;
spread it, you could spread it to someone who is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:38.960 --> 00:05:44.320
in a more compromised position. And although&nbsp;
that's the situation with the Delta variant,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:44.320 --> 00:05:49.120
the more people remain unvaccinated in the more&nbsp;
the spread continues. The next variant could be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:49.120 --> 00:05:53.600
more deadly. The next variant could be even&nbsp;
more transmissible. And as we've said before,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:53.600 --> 00:05:58.400
imagine if this had an eight percent mortality&nbsp;
rate or a 10 percent mortality rate. If&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:58.400 --> 00:06:02.560
I don't know that people are looking to read&nbsp;
about this type of stuff right now, I don't know.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:02.560 --> 00:06:07.680
People are looking for this type of fiction. But&nbsp;
I recently read Lawrence Wright's pandemic novel,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:09.200 --> 00:06:14.640
I believe is called The End of October, where&nbsp;
it's a very similar situation to the one we have,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:14.640 --> 00:06:19.360
except it's like a 10 percent death rate instead&nbsp;
of up zero point eight percent death rate or&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:19.360 --> 00:06:24.800
whatever. We believe the real infection fatality&nbsp;
rate to be, that is a dramatically different&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:24.800 --> 00:06:30.480
situation. The more we don't get vaccinated and&nbsp;
the more this continues to spread, it increases&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:30.480 --> 00:06:35.360
the chances of such a variant developing in the&nbsp;
future. So these are the rules at this point in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:35.360 --> 00:06:42.160
time. People asking me if I'm if I'm canceling my&nbsp;
upcoming travel. I'm not. And the reason I'm not&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:42.160 --> 00:06:50.560
is this situation of different pops and spreads,&nbsp;
particularly among the unvaccinated, is likely to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:50.560 --> 00:06:59.920
continue for a couple of years. And so if I'm not&nbsp;
willing to travel now, I probably shouldn't travel&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:59.920 --> 00:07:06.320
for years. And I've made the decision in speaking&nbsp;
with friends who are doctors and others that right&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:06.320 --> 00:07:10.880
now, based on when I got vaccinated and based&nbsp;
on this particular variant and based on the fact&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:10.880 --> 00:07:16.320
that I'll be wearing a mask everywhere that it's&nbsp;
recommended, I don't see a particular reason to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:16.320 --> 00:07:22.480
cancel that trip now. But a lot of the questions&nbsp;
are where are you going and what is your health&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:22.480 --> 00:07:29.120
status, et cetera. One example we're talking on&nbsp;
the bonus show today, Nevada or Nevada is going&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:29.120 --> 00:07:34.960
fully mask back on and people are being advised to&nbsp;
avoid Las Vegas. The level of uncontrolled spread&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:34.960 --> 00:07:40.880
in Las Vegas is so high, the case positivity&nbsp;
rate is so high that that's a point where people&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:40.880 --> 00:07:46.160
are being told, just don't go there and I don't&nbsp;
plan to. So that's that's the situation there.

